      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew around the Chicago, Burlington and Quincy Railroad, which brought merchants and shifted commerce from nearby Coldbrook.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cameron_illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1996 a connection track was built between the former Burlington Northern line and the former Santa Fe Chillicothe Subdivision, allowing Amtrak\u2019s Southwest Chief to use the Chicago\u2013Mendota route through Cameron.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
